,{"id":"marker80","name":"Semesh Monster","legend":"Whispers say a relic monster of 5 m long inhabits Semesh Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker81","name":"Hordh Monster","legend":"Elders say a relic monster of 23 m long inhabits Hordh Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker82","name":"Nibamara Monster","legend":"Whispers say a relic monster of 5 m long inhabits Nibamara Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker83","name":"Shushahtar Monster","legend":"Journeying folk say a relic monster of 11 m long inhabits Shushahtar Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker84","name":"Waton Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 51 m long."},{"id":"marker85","name":"Skiping Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 21 m long."},{"id":"marker86","name":"Manch Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 32 m long."},{"id":"marker87","name":"Soles Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 26 m long."},{"id":"marker88","name":"Hausach Vampire","legend":"Tipplers speak of a huge Vampire who inhabits Hausach hills and eats kids whole."},{"id":"marker89","name":"Hepehatom Dragon","legend":"Tales speak of a proud Dragon who inhabits Hepehatom hills and attacks anyone who dares to approach its lair."},{"id":"marker90","name":"Kehyon Banshee","legend":"Legends speak of a giant Banshee who inhabits Kehyon hills and snatches people from homes."},{"id":"marker91","name":"Ebrongengen Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Witnesses of Schofenbach."},{"id":"marker92","name":"Otyery Palm Grove","legend":"A palm grove sacred to